title The day that had not started
prompt The baton -- take the next agent-doable lap, reds first.
rota lap 4171, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; the air threshold asks a lap to press each boundary and see whether the hand passes through. It did here: a census whose fence was "today" had no post standing at midnight.
think Cold roster open answered guards_red=3 -- index_row_bound on one misordered shelf row, and standing_equipment reading its own roster's red. Reds first, so that closed before new work: tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh sorts the row block, proving its output is a permutation of its input before it writes.
think The card named rota_declared reds every midnight as mine. The scan took DAY from TZ=America/New_York date and read that shelf with git ls-files, which reads the INDEX -- so between 00:00 and the day's first committed log the corpus was empty and it exited 2.
think It was right about the corpus (REDS %170: a corpus of zero is a red, never a reading) and wrong about the subject. An empty subject and an absent subject are two readings.
think The repair keeps %170 whole rather than weakening it: the reported day is always a day that HOLDS tracked logs. The open day falls back to the newest shelf that does, walking shelf names on disk in descending order so no date arithmetic enters, bounded at seven shelves.
think A day a caller NAMES is not rescued -- ROTA_DAY asked about that day and is owed the refusal. day_source=open|fallback|asked prints beside day=, so the two readings are told apart.
obs The cost was never one guard's red. A red guard withholds the roster receipt, so --scoped refuses and eight ships each pay a full cold pass -- nightly, healed an hour later by the first commit, which reads as somebody's fault and then vanishes.
obs Booked and closed in one lap: REDS %567, folded to its own shelf; the ledger headline moved 563 to 564 and its derived remainder 543 to 544, since the monotone witness refuses a headline that disagrees with the spine it measures.
obs Number booked after git fetch xy, and xy had moved three commits with rows %561-%563; the fast-forward landed before the fold, so %567 was still free. The recital conflicted on the stash pop and was resolved by keeping both sides in stamp order.
obs The hot pass caught two of my own before the commit: `fold_shelf_link` red because the folded account kept the `archive/` prefix of the card it left, and `vocabulary_collection` red because my box wrote a word the tree retired for reader-facing prose, three times. Both green after repair.
obs Two reds stand that are not this lap's and not this lane's: `stash_record` reads 21 orphaned round-open stashes holding unlanded session logs, and `fleet_watch`'s tmux control fails one of sixteen on a timing leg. Named rather than routed around.
loom witness=rota_declared_witness control_cases=18 scan_logs=56 rota_field=52 prose_only=2 silent=2
loom roster=cold_open guards_run=170 guards_seconds=1362 guards_green=164 guards_red=3
file tools/fixtures/r/rota_declared_scan.sh the fallback walk, the bound, and day_source
file tools/fixtures/r/rota_declared_control.sh seven new cases: both halves of midnight, the named-day refusal, the bound
file tools/r/rota_declared_witness.rish control 11 to 18, and day_source asserted reported
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the roster entry's prose, repaired rather than describing a standing fault
file construction/REDS.md headline 563 to 564; the row itself folded to its shelf
file construction/archive/REDS-the-day-that-had-not-started-rows-564.md the closed row, one click away
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Patchouli box; the elder account shelved
recommend keep-going the several-line interleave in mantra/src/weave.rye is the lane's real next door -- it wants an anchor per insert, which widens Diff and is a seam rather than a lap, so the door beside it is smaller: nothing in the tree yet reads day_source, and the roster could.
